IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hesa-help`

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth), HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP, HELP debts and their repayment, from the student's seat -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_higher-education-support-act-2003_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts: Chloe enrols in a Bachelor of Commerce at UWA on 22 February 2021 (c030), has taxable income of $27,500 for
-- 2023-24 (c045) and $71,500 for 2024-25 (c048); Daniel enrols in a Bachelor of Commerce at UWA on 24 February 2014 (d020) and
-- a Juris Doctor on 27 February 2017 (d022). Census dates, contribution amounts, loans, balances, debts and indexation factors
-- are HYPOTHETICAL unless a comment says they come from the Act or the scenario.

`Chloe, Commerce at UWA, 2021` MEANS Enrolment WITH
    `status` IS `an Australian citizen`
    `will be resident in Australia for the unit` IS TRUE
    `meets the New Zealand special category test` IS FALSE
    `holds a permanent visa` IS FALSE
    `provider expects no units in Australia` IS FALSE
    `provider has a funding agreement for the year` IS TRUE
    `Table A provider` IS TRUE
    `unit is within a funded national priority` IS FALSE
    `unit contributes to the course` IS TRUE
    `assessed as academically suited` IS TRUE
