§ `ss 36-5, 36-10 -- Am I a Commonwealth supported student`

#ASSERT `Do the student identifier requirements apply to me` `Chloe, Commerce at UWA, 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Do the student identifier requirements apply to me` `Daniel, Commerce at UWA, 2014`

#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the student identifier condition` `Chloe, had she not notified a student identifier`

#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a Commonwealth supported place` `a New Zealand citizen resident here, 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a Commonwealth supported place` `an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder on a temporary visa, 2024`

-- c030 (Chloe) and d020 (Daniel); d022: the Juris Doctor is Commonwealth supported only if UWA advised it in writing.
#ASSERT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `Chloe, Commerce at UWA, 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `Chloe, had she not notified a student identifier`
#ASSERT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `Daniel, Commerce at UWA, 2014`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `Daniel, Juris Doctor at UWA, 2017, not advised`
#ASSERT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `a permanent visa holder, 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `a student who opted out, 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `a citizen whose provider expects no units in Australia, 2024`

§ `ss 90-1, 90-5, 104-1, 104-5 -- HECS-HELP or FEE-HELP`

#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a HELP loan` `a permanent visa holder, 2024`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a HELP loan` `a New Zealand citizen meeting the special category test, 2024`

-- c030: Chloe on HECS-HELP. d020: Daniel on HECS-HELP.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `Chloe, Commerce at UWA, 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `Chloe, had she not notified a student identifier`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `Daniel, Commerce at UWA, 2014`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `Daniel, Juris Doctor, had UWA advised him`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `a permanent visa holder, 2024`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` `a permanent humanitarian visa holder, 2024`

-- d022: Daniel's Juris Doctor on FEE-HELP.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` `Daniel, Juris Doctor at UWA, 2017, not advised`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` `Daniel, Juris Doctor, had UWA advised him`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` `Daniel, Juris Doctor, had he studied it at an overseas campus`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` `a student at a non-Table A provider outside a national priority, 2024`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` `an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder on a temporary visa, 2024`

§ `ss 93-1, 93-10, 93-20 -- What is deferred`

-- c030: the most a commerce place can cost, as the s 93-10 table states it.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be charged for a place` `law, accounting, administration, economics or commerce` EQUALS 14500

#ASSERT `How much HECS-HELP assistance do I get for the unit` 3625 0 106319 EQUALS 3625
#ASSERT `How much HECS-HELP assistance do I get for the unit` 3625 0 2000 EQUALS 2000

-- s 93-20(2), the Act's own example (Kate).
#ASSERT `How much HELP assistance do I get for units with one census date` 2400 2000 EQUALS 2000

-- s 93-5(1), (4): a hypothetical $16,992 a place, a unit of 0.0833 EFTSL: $1,415.43 rounds down to $1,415.
#ASSERT `What is my student contribution amount for the unit` 16992 0.0833 EQUALS 1415

