§ `ss 137-5, 137-10, 137-19A -- What becomes a HELP debt`

#ASSERT `Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20 per cent` 20241231
#ASSERT NOT `Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20 per cent` 20250601

-- c030: a 2021 unit, no cut.
#ASSERT `What HECS-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` 3625 20250331 EQUALS 2900
#ASSERT `What HECS-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` 3625 20210331 EQUALS 3625

-- d022: a postgraduate FEE-HELP loan carries no loan fee.
#ASSERT `What FEE-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` 20000 FALSE FALSE 20170331 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `What FEE-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` 10000 FALSE TRUE 20170331 EQUALS 12500
#ASSERT `What FEE-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` 10000 FALSE TRUE 20250331 EQUALS 9600

§ `ss 140-5, 140-10, 140-25, 140-26, 140-30 -- How my debt grows`

#ASSERT `What indexation factor applies to my HELP debt` 1.038 1.041 EQUALS 1.038

-- s 140-5, the Act's own example (Lorraine), and the same facts in the financial year starting 1 July 2024 (s 140-26(1)).
#ASSERT `What is my former accumulated HELP debt` 15000 1500 525 3000 0 0 1.030 FALSE EQUALS 13364.25
#ASSERT `What is my former accumulated HELP debt` 15000 1500 525 3000 0 0 1.030 TRUE EQUALS 10691.4

-- s 140-25, the Act's own example (Paula), and s 140-30 rounding.
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated HELP debt` 20000 1500 0 0 EQUALS 21500
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated HELP debt` 13364.25 0 0 0 EQUALS 13364

-- s 140-26(2): Lorraine's cut former debt $10,691.40, $3,000 incurred, $500 repaid: $10,691.40 + $2,000 = $12,691 (s 140-30).
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated HELP debt on 1 June 2025` 10691.4 3000 500 0 EQUALS 12691

§ `ss 151-1, 151-10, 151-15 -- Paying it off early`

#ASSERT `May I make a voluntary repayment` TRUE

#ASSERT `How much of my repayment goes to my accumulated HELP debt` 6000 5000 EQUALS 5000

#ASSERT `How much of my repayment goes to my newer HELP debts` 6000 5000 3000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `How much of my repayment goes to my newer HELP debts` 1000 5000 3000 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `How much of my repayment is refunded to me` 10000 8000 500 EQUALS 1500

§ `ss 154-1 to 154-25 -- When must I repay, and how much`

-- c045 (2023-24) and c048 (2024-25) fall before 2025-26: the deposited text does not state their thresholds.
#ASSERT `Which repayment thresholds apply to my income year` 2025 EQUALS `the thresholds the compiled text states`
#ASSERT `Which repayment thresholds apply to my income year` 2024 EQUALS `a repealed rule that is not in the deposit`

-- s 154-25: hypothetical AWE of $2,000 against $1,900 for 2025-26: $67,000 x 2000/1900 = $70,526.32, rounded down.
#ASSERT `What does an indexable amount become` 67000 2000 1900 EQUALS 70526

#ASSERT `What is my minimum repayment income` 2025 0 EQUALS JUST 67000
#ASSERT `What is my minimum repayment income` 2024 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- c045: $27,500, no Medicare levy -- no repayment. c048: $71,500 against the compiled $67,000 -- liable (see NOTES).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I make a compulsory repayment` 27500 67000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I make a compulsory repayment` 71500 67000 TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I make a compulsory repayment` 67000 67000 TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- c048 read against the compiled 2025-26 rule: 15% of $4,500 = $675; the 10% cap ($7,150) does not bind.
#ASSERT `How much is my compulsory repayment` 71500 67000 125000 20000 EQUALS 675
#ASSERT `How much is my compulsory repayment` 200000 67000 125000 50000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `How much is my compulsory repayment` 100000 67000 125000 3000 EQUALS 3000

#ASSERT `What is my repayable debt` 20000 675 EQUALS 19325

§ `ss 137-20, 140-40 -- If I die`

#ASSERT `If I die how much of my HELP debts can still be collected` 25000 3000 675 EQUALS 675
#ASSERT `If I die how much of my HELP debts can still be collected` 25000 3000 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 154-18(1) -- Leaving Australia`

-- Daniel's later year in London (not one of this Act's plan events): a debtor leaving for 183 days or more must tell the ATO.
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Commissioner that I have left Australia` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I notify the Commissioner that I have left Australia` TRUE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Within how many days after leaving must I notify the Commissioner`  EQUALS 7

